WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.636
-The president threatened Iran
on Twitter over the weekend

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:06.672
as the people around him
seem to push for a conflict.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.442
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:13.580
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.282
You might remember that,
during the 2016 campaign,

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.719
Donald Trump pretended
he was the anti-war candidate,

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.721
lying about his
position on the Iraq war,

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.755
and calling it
a "mistake."

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.657
Although,
if you paid close attention,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.593
it really seems like
he had an ulterior motive.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:32.832
-Obviously, the war in Iraq
was a big, fat mistake, alright?

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.868
George Bush made a mistake.
We can make mistakes.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.269
But that one was a beauty.

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:39.272
We should have never
been in Iraq.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.440
We have destabilized
the Middle East.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.175
-Had we not
done anything --

00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:46.779
had our politicians gone to
the beach and enjoyed the sun --

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:49.248
we would be in a lot better
position than we are right now.

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:50.883
What we've done
is incredible.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.585
If we would have --
if our presidents

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.622
would have just stayed home
and gone to the beach,

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:58.258
or even gone and played golf
every single day --

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:02.061
played two rounds a day,
okay?

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:05.064
-Well, that's one promise
he definitely kept.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.198
I mean...

00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:07.367
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.803
So, --
So, the president...

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.805
The president spent
the 2016 campaign

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.707
branding himself
as the anti-war candidate.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.408
And then, on Sunday,
he jumped on Twitter

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:19.012
to threaten a war with Iran --
seemingly out of nowhere.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.080
-Just in to CNN,
President Trump tweeting

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.915
this stern warning
to Iran.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.383
"If Iran wants to fight,

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.519
that will be the official end
of Iran.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.221
Never threaten
the United States again."

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:32.225
-I can't believe I'm saying
this, but go play golf.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.426
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:35.328
It's actually now
a matter of national security

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.196
that we make sure
Trump spends as much time

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:38.430
on the golf course
as possible.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.132
Otherwise,
he'll spend his time

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.700
threatening to start wars
on Twitter.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.170
We need one of those
Homeland Security threat meters

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.239
that tells us how much golf
he needs to play

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.373
based on his mood.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.974
Low -- sit in cart.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:50.676
Guarded --
driving range.

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:53.278
Elevated -- practice putting
while sitting in cart.

00:01:53.278 --> 00:01:55.982
High -- one round with B-list
celebrity, like Kid Rock.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.617
Severe -- two full rounds,
and trick him into thinking

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.053
he's trapped in the sand
all day

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.354
by tossing a new ball into the
bunker ever time he hits it

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:05.358
until he digs himself a hole
and falls asleep in it.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.727
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.896 --> 00:02:13.432
Trump cast himself as
the anti-war candidate,

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:15.334
and now, he's tweeting
threats of war.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.503
And on top of that, he's
surrounding himself with aides

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:18.905
who have repeatedly
called for war --

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:20.873
like his National Security
Adviser, John Bolton,

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.308
who championed
the Iraq War.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.211
Bolton has publicly called
for bombing Iran, North Korea,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.713
and Syria, and a former
Trump Administration official

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:30.917
once told the New Yorker,
"John wants to bomb everyone."

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.653
And it's not exactly reassuring
to know that this is the guy

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.088
advising Trump, because Trump
is very impressionable.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.424
He's like your dip[bleep] son
who starts hanging around

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.159
with a bunch of
high-school burnouts.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:41.360
"Why do you have
a nose ring,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.496
and where did you get
this bag of weed?"

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.697
[ As Trump ]
"John gave it to me,

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.365
and I smoked the weed
because John told me

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.201
drugs are cool, Mom."

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.902
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.739
[ Normal voice ]
In fact, Bolton is so pro-war
that Trump said recently

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.741
he actually keeps Bolton
in check.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.843
-Are you satisfied
with the advice you receive

00:02:57.843 --> 00:02:59.312
from John Bolton?

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.480
-Yeah.
John's very good.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.949
John is a, uh...

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.217
He has strong views on things,
but that's okay.

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:08.754
I actually temper John, which is
pretty amazing, isn't it?

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:10.757
-Even Trump knows
how crazy it is

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.592
that he's
the voice of reason.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.793
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.094
I mean, think about
what he's saying there.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:19.698
That joke only works if everyone
knows Trump is crazy.

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:20.733
He's basically saying,

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:21.734
[ As Trump ]
"Sure, I'm a nutjob,

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.369
But you should see
this guy."

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.539
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.407
[ Normal voice ]
It's like getting...

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:31.544
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.680
It's like getting in
a fist fight at a bar

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.514
and having it broken up
by Conor McGregor.

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.716
[ In Irish accent ] "Guy, guys,
let's settle this with words.

00:03:37.716 --> 00:03:40.353
Words, not violence.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.488
And I'm certain
this is how I talk."

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.924
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.225
[ Normal voice ]
Now, it was reported last week

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:48.694
that Trump is actually
frustrated with how quickly

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.029
his pro-war advisers,

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.864
like Bolton and
Secretary of State Mike Pompeo,

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.999
are moving towards
a conflict with Iran.

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.567
Trump tried to tamp down
those reports

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.069
of in-fighting
within his administration,

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.005
tweeting that "different
opinions are expressed,

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.140
and I make a decisive
and final decision."

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.243
So, there you go. Trump makes
the decisive and final decision.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.278
And yet, he still acts like
he doesn't have control

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:07.547
over his own
administration.

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.415
The next day, for example,
he was asked by reporters

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.550
outside the White House

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.351
if we were headed toward
a war with Iran,

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:15.721
and his response
was not very reassuring.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:19.058
-Mr. President,
are we going to war with Iran?

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.326
-I hope not.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.229
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.931
-What ha-- Wait.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:28.067
What happened to
decisive decisions?

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.703
"I hope not" isn't an answer
to war with Iran.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:33.473
It's an answer to the question
"Do you think it's gonna rain?"

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.107
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.107 --> 00:04:39.345
Also, Trump is waiting for the
Swiss delegation in that clip,

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.580
but still,
why does he just stand there

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.749
in the doorway to
the White House like that?

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:46.151
He's like a retiree
who sits on his porch all day

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:48.387
waiting for the mail
to arrive.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.423
[ As Trump ] "Let's see.
Mail usually comes at noon.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:53.159
Right now, it's 6:00 a.m.
I'd better get out there."

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:54.427
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.628
[ Normal voice ]
The other problem here is,

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.963
we don't know whose interests
Trump is serving.

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:00.400
On one hand,
he says he doesn't want war.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.801
But on the other hand, he's
listening to guys like Bolton,

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:04.436
who has openly called
for regime change.

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:07.340
And then, there's Saudi Arabia,
which is fighting a proxy war

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:08.741
with Iran
in the Middle East.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.709
We don't know what Trump's
financial relationship

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:11.711
with Saudi Arabia
is like

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.879
because he won't release
his tax returns.

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.347
But in the past,
he's bragged about

00:05:15.347 --> 00:05:17.316
his financial relationships
with Saudis.

00:05:17.316 --> 00:05:19.685
-I love the Saudis.
Many are in this building.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:22.421
Saudi Arabia -- And I get along
great with all of them.

00:05:22.421 --> 00:05:23.589
They buy apartments
from me.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.424
They spend $40 million,
$50 million.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:26.625
Am I supposed to
dislike them?

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.828
I like them
very much.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.030
-"They give me money,
so I like them"

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.533
is the literal definition
of bribery.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.337
So, Trump and his team --
Trump and his team...

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:41.640
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.075
...they keep sending
mixed signals.

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:44.477
In fact,
it was reported last week

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.579
that the intelligence suggests
the U.S. an Iran

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:49.748
might actually be misreading
each other's stoking tensions.

00:05:49.748 --> 00:05:52.017
And yet, Trump complained that
it was actually the media

00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:53.486
that was getting
the story wrong,

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:56.355
while also bragging that it was
good to keep Iran guessing.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:58.156
-The president posted,
quote,

00:05:58.156 --> 00:06:00.659
"With all the fake
and made-up news out there,

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:04.430
Iran can have no idea
what is actually going on."

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:07.533
-"The fake news media is hurting
our country with its fraudulent

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.902
and highly inaccurate
coverage of Iran.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:11.837
It is scattershot,
poorly sourced,

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.439
made up, and dangerous.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.741
At least Iran doesn't know
what to think --

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.544
which, at this point,
may very well be a good thing."

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:19.712
-No, it's not.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:22.481
Unpredictability
is not a good thing.

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:25.718
Unpredictability is one of
the symptoms of rabies.

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:27.720
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.388
The fundamental problem
is that Trump has

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:32.325
no consistent worldview, and has
no idea what he's talking about.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:33.692
He just listens
to the TV.

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:35.060
Trump basically
only hired Bolton

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:37.229
because he saw Bolton
on Fox News all the time.

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:39.331
In fact, Bolton even went
on Fox News last year,

00:06:39.331 --> 00:06:42.334
and insisted that the invasion
of Iraq was a success,

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:44.971
it was just everything that came
after it that was bad.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.906
-I think the overthrow
of Saddam Hussein --

00:06:47.906 --> 00:06:51.777
that military action --
was a resounding success.

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:55.014
I think the mistakes that were
made subsequently --

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.617
setting up the coalition
provisional authority,

00:06:57.617 --> 00:07:00.119
and others that
followed from it --

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:04.257
are lessons about what to do
after a regime is overthrown.

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.258
-Oh, I see.
So, invading Iraq worked out.

00:07:06.258 --> 00:07:09.094
It's just everything that
happened because of it was bad.

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:10.963
That's like if you went
to Vegas, got drunk,

00:07:10.963 --> 00:07:12.765
and eloped with first person
you met,

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:14.600
and then said,
"The wedding itself was great.

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.202
It's just all the sobering up,
and having no shared interests

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:19.071
beyond alcoholism
that ruined things."

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.339
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:22.307
We've been here before. We can't
repeat the same mistakes

00:07:22.307 --> 00:07:23.476
that led to
the war in Iraq.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.444
Trump's team seems to be
pushing for a conflict

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:27.579
despite resistance
from basically everybody.

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:29.916
I don't know if they'll succeed,
but all I can say is...

00:07:29.916 --> 00:07:31.384
-I hope not.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:33.552
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:37.557
[ Cheers and applause ]

